[282.970765, "o", "> "]
[282.97104, "o", "The project's pom.xml has profile definitions that check for the existence of tools.jar:"]
[282.971079, "o", "\r\n"]
[282.971116, "o", "> "]
[282.971324, "o", "  - default-profile: checks for ${java.home}/../lib/tools.jar (Linux/Windows)"]
[282.971381, "o", "\r\n> "]
[282.971572, "o", "  - mac-profile: checks for ${java.home}/../Classes/classes.jar (macOS)"]
[282.971623, "o", "\r\n"]
[282.971646, "o", "> \r\n"]
[282.971684, "o", "> "]
[282.972496, "o", "In Java 9+, tools.jar was removed and its contents were merged into the main JDK modules. The file no longer exists at the expected location. However, the parent pom (auto-parent v3) defines a toolsjar property that is used somewhere as a system-scoped dependency with com.sun:tools.\r\n"]
[282.972533, "o", "> "]
[282.972544, "o", "\r\n"]
[282.972569, "o", "> "]
[282.973089, "o", "When the profile activation fails (because tools.jar doesn't exist), the toolsjar property is not set, but Maven still tries to resolve the com.sun:tools dependency that references this property, causing the build to fail.\r\n"]
[282.973116, "o", "> \r\n"]
[282.97313, "o", "> "]
[282.973179, "o", "ERROR LOCATION:\r\n"]
[282.973195, "o", "> "]
[282.973329, "o", "- File: pom.xml (parent pom.xml in the root directory)\r\n"]
[282.973357, "o", "> "]
[282.973476, "o", "- Lines: Profile definitions around lines 163-208\r\n"]
[282.9735, "o", "> \r\n"]
[282.97355, "o", "> SOLUTION:\r\n"]
[282.973586, "o", "> "]
[282.973897, "o", "The fix is to update the profile activation logic to handle Java 9+ properly. Since tools.jar no longer exists in Java 9+, we should:\r\n"]
[282.973914, "o", "> "]
[282.974067, "o", "1. Remove or make optional the dependency on com.sun:tools\r\n"]
[282.974086, "o", "> "]
[282.974266, "o", "2. Update the profile activation to not fail when tools.jar doesn't exist\r\n"]
[282.974285, "o", "> "]
[282.974546, "o", "3. For Java 9+, tools.jar is not needed as the compiler has built-in support for all necessary functionality\r\n"]
[282.974571, "o", "> \r\n"]
[282.974587, "o", "> "]
[282.974681, "o", "The profile should be modified to:\r\n"]
[282.974739, "o", "> "]
[282.974868, "o", "- Not activate by default on Java 9+ (where tools.jar doesn't exist)\r\n"]
[282.974906, "o", "> "]
[282.975078, "o", "- Only activate on Java 8 and earlier (where tools.jar is available)\r\n"]
[282.975099, "o", "> EOF\r\n"]
[282.976544, "o", "root@a59b4aa9fbc3:/home/travis/build/failed/google/auto# "]
[282.976666, "o", "cat /home/travis/build/failed/failed_reasons.txt\r\n"]
[282.977636, "o", "Build Error Analysis for Google Auto Repository\r\n================================================\r\n\r\nERROR DESCRIPTION:\r\nThe build fails with the following error:\r\n  \"Could not find artifact com.sun:tools:jar:11.0.27 at specified path /usr/lib/jvm/java-11-openjdk-amd64/../lib/tools.jar\"\r\n\r\nROOT CAUSE:\r\nThe project's pom.xml has profile definitions that check for the existence of tools.jar:\r\n  - default-profile: checks for ${java.home}/../lib/tools.jar (Linux/Windows)\r\n  - mac-profile: checks for ${java.home}/../Classes/classes.jar (macOS)\r\n\r\nIn Java 9+, tools.jar was removed and its contents were merged into the main JDK modules. The file no longer exists at the expected location. However, the parent pom (auto-parent v3) defines a toolsjar property that is used somewhere as a system-scoped dependency with com.sun:tools.\r\n\r\nWhen the profile activation fails (because tools.jar doesn't exist), the toolsjar property is not set, but Maven still tries to resolve the com.sun:tools dependency that references this pro"]
[282.977666, "o", "perty, causing the build to fail.\r\n\r\nERROR LOCATION:\r\n- File: pom.xml (parent pom.xml in the root directory)\r\n- Lines: Profile definitions around lines 163-208\r\n\r\nSOLUTION:\r\nThe fix is to update the profile activation logic to handle Java 9+ properly. Since tools.jar no longer exists in Java 9+, we should:\r\n1. Remove or make optional the dependency on com.sun:tools\r\n2. Update the profile activation to not fail when tools.jar doesn't exist\r\n3. For Java 9+, tools.jar is not needed as the compiler has built-in support for all necessary functionality\r\n\r\nThe profile should be modified to:\r\n- Not activate by default on Java 9+ (where tools.jar doesn't exist)\r\n- Only activate on Java 8 and earlier (where tools.jar is available)\r\n"]
[282.977785, "o", "root@a59b4aa9fbc3:/home/travis/build/failed/google/auto# "]
[288.258795, "i", "cd /home/travis/build/failed/google/auto && cat > patch_1.diff << 'EOF'\n--- a/pom.xml\n+++ b/pom.xml\n@@ -163,9 +163,6 @@\n   <profile>\n    <id>\n     default-profile\n    </id>\n    <activation>\n-    <activeByDefault>\n-     true\n-    </activeByDefault>\n     <file>\n      <exists>\n       ${java.home}/../lib/tools.jar\nEOF\ncat patch_1.diff\n"]
